1747 1088 \nQ 2099 262 2266 262 \nQ 2400 262 2554 531 \nQ 2586 582 2650 698 \nL 2746 627 \nQ 2522 224 2374 77 \nQ 2227 -70 2035 -70 \nQ 1894 -70 1782 42 \nQ 1670 154 1517 454 \nQ 1325 826 1133 1357 \nL 877 1152 \nL 570 0 \nL 90 0 \nL 992 3379 \nQ 1082 3699 1107 3942 \nQ 1088 4096 781 4096 \nL 666 4096 \nL 666 4198 \nQ 1146 4256 1670 4371 \nL 1709 4333 \nL 941 1414 \nL 1216 1626 \nQ 2131 2330 2131 2522 \nQ 2131 2637 1894 2637 \nL 1805 2637 \nL 1805 2739 \nL 2950 2739 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-6b\" transform=\"translate(0 0.703125)\"></use></g></g><g id=\"text_9\"><!-- $\\mathit{t}$ --><g transform=\"translate(16.711364 16.011562) scale(0.13 -0.13)\"><defs><path id=\"STIXGeneral-Italic-74\" d=\"M 1894 2739 \nL 1862 2534 \nL 1325 2534 \nL 768 435 \nQ 755 384 755 346 \nQ 755 243 851 243 \nQ 928 243 1030 342 \nQ 1133 442 1370 749 \nL 1453 704 \nQ 1158 256 969 93 \nQ 781 -70 538 -70 \nQ 243 -70 243 166 \nQ 243 230 346 640 \nL 845 2534 \nL 365 2534 \nL 358 2573 \nQ 358 2688 570 2733 \nQ 730 2771 992 2979 \nQ 1254 3187 1421 3437 \nQ 1459 3494 1510 3494 \nQ 1568 3494 1568 3443 \nQ 1568 3411 1562 3398 \nL 1382 2739 \nL 1894 2739 \nz\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"></path></defs><use xlink:href=\"#STIXGeneral-Italic-74\" transform=\"translate(0 0.40625)\"></use></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p2130b2d5fd\"><rect x=\"7.2\" y=\"13.078804\" width=\"209.25\" height=\"207.9\"></rect></clipPath></defs></svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 3 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled t, j, and k.</li><li>Line t intersects both line j and line k.</li><li>At the intersection of line t and line j, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br><ul><li>Top right: w°</li><li>Bottom left: 134°</li></ul></li><li>At the intersection of line t and line k, 3 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br><ul><li>Top left: x°</li><li>Top right: y°</li><li>Bottom right: z°</li></ul></li><li>Note: Figure not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure, line <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> intersects lines <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that lines <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> are parallel?</p>", "keys": ["69642998-98a2-4505-912c-0037f2c8ae88"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "69642998-98a2-4505-912c-0037f2c8ae88", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"x equals 46\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>46</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "eacf750e-c2a4-475a-8a88-a54ab57f59ad", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"y equals 46\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>46</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "8b845693-e755-4973-b3e2-ad1a52c28858", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"w equals 134\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>134</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "2aa59e61-838f-443d-9610-dec56fce40db", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"z equals 134\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>z</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>134</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. In the figure shown, line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math>, which is a transversal, intersects lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>. If two lines are intersected by a transversal and the measures of a pair of same-side interior angles sum to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, then the lines are parallel. In the figure, the angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"134 degree\"><mn>134</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are a pair of same-side interior angles. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 46\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>46</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 134 plus x right parenthesis degree  equals left parenthesis 134 plus 46 right parenthesis degree\"><mo>(</mo><mn>134</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>134</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>46</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 134 plus x right parenthesis degree  equals 180 degree\"><mo>(</mo><mn>134</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 46\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>46</mn></math>&nbsp;is sufficient to prove that lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y degree\"><mi>y</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"134 degree\"><mn>134</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are alternate interior angles. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 46\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>46</mn></math> rather than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 134\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>134</mn></math>, then lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> would not be parallel.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"134 degree\"><mn>134</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> are vertical angles. Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w equals 134\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>134</mn></math>&nbsp;whether lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel or not.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "275a2867-6329-41e4-8bab-072a1e2475e7", "correct_answer": ["A"]}